t. | adjudicated | 2026-08-23 |\n| [[connections/keep-it-retrievable-not-resident]] | On-ramp distillation and Tier A index trimming are the same lever applied at different layers: cut standing per-session context, never the retrievable corpus or the permanent output. | adjudicated | 2026-08-30 |\n| [[connections/git-repository-boundaries-should-be-explicit]] | A stray home-directory `.git` and near-committed nested worktrees are the same inferred-boundary failure in opposite directions; both fixes replace inference with an explicit declaration. | adjudicated | 2026-08-30 |\n| [[connections/git-scope-errors-inflate-the-work-estimate]] | Phantom 10k changes and a 235-occurrence rewrite were both accurate counts against the wrong git frame — check repo root and remote authority before acting on any bulk count | adjudicated | 2026-08-30 |\n| [[concepts/backup-manifest-drift-and-launchd-status-lag]] | Backup manifest omission (3 project folders) as a distinct `backup-error` class; `launchctl list` column 2 reports only the last scheduled run, so a stale red exit code self-clears and should be left alone | 2026-08-31.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[concepts/stale-error-log-archival-discipline]] | `.errors.log` is an append-only escalation channel, not a state record; entries must be confirmed stale against an independent source, then archived before clearing | 2026-08-31.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[connections/status-field-scope-narrower-than-the-question]] | launchd's scheduled-run-only exit code and self-counting comment bumps both report accurately on a narrower predicate than the operational question; check the field's scope before concluding it lied | 2026-08-31.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[concepts/dev-knowledge-graph-refresh-2026]] | Adds the quota-strategy and compiler-backlog cross-links alongside the ARMS gaps and scratch-folder references | 2026-09-01.md | 2026-09-01 |\n| [[concepts/codex-adversarial-verification]] | Adds the preregistration and reviewer-unavailability cross-link